pe\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"4a7b8f95c60bd4083a093c9a0fbef8dd04bbdf2646b2ee6e1cab5c3f8eceaa3d","event_uuid":"0b1b24a9-3320-47d0-b333-4e1f6f1070f9","position":{"commit_sha":"b8bb78bbe362645feb4e81dbc9f3e779f901897e","position":"1786326725561330001-0b1b24a9-3320-47d0-b333-4e1f6f1070f9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 RCA — confirmed defect (no repair performed yet)\n\nProven root cause: every cumulative-counter block in infra/scripts/observability.sh persists its offset as soon as the source total is observed, before aws cloudwatch put-metric-data acknowledges delivery (replication 101-108; voter 130-138; merge 153-159; deploy 174-180; shared deferral/interrupt helper 203-212; G2P 252-260). The persisted offset is an acknowledgement cursor, so a failed publish followed by the same cumulative total computes zero and permanently excludes the failed positive delta. The ticket omitted G2P; it is the same copied construct.\n\nDiscriminating runtime proof: a whole-script PATH-shim experiment parameterized all seven metric streams across six code shapes. Each began with offset 2 and source total 7; the targeted first AWS call exited 23. In every case the script exited 0 and the offset became 7. The next successful run published value 0, while retaining offset 2 would publish 5. All 9 probes passed, including both shared-helper metrics, G2P, and a reset control (offset 10/source 7 produced failed 7 then successful 0). Removing only 2>/dev/null || true still produced 5 then 0, proving suppression hides the loss but is not a second necessary cause. A zero delta has no positive count to acknowledge and is a negative control, not a separate behavior change. Temporary instrumentation was removed after the experiment.\n\nDefect legitimacy: defect. The original stories require observed replication, voter, merge-path, deploy, review-interrupt, and G2P failures to publish metrics and trip their alarms (spiny-micro-ladle; cogent-strut-kid; elfish-chair-lug; gall-plume-adder; equestrian-clueless-cowbird; smoky-flare-slug). Current Terraform contracts define these as per-period new-error counts. No authority permits discarding a detected count after transient CloudWatch failure.\n\nCaller-dependency gate: expected behavior is that offsets advance only after the matching AWS call succeeds; on failure they remain byte-identical so the next run retries the accumulated delta. The script is installed by install-observability.sh/systemd and refreshed by autodeploy; tests and runbooks consume its metrics but no caller depends on premature acknowledgement. All affected metrics share the same contract. No behavioral-dependency blocker.","timestamp":1786300511594168001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final rebar-debug report\n\nProblem: cumulative observability counters acknowledged their offsets before CloudWatch accepted the corresponding datapoint, permanently dropping the failed interval.\n\nProven root cause: all seven streams across six code shapes persisted the observed total before the matching aws cloudwatch put-metric-data call. Because the offset is the acknowledgement cursor, a transient publish failure made the next run compute zero from an already-advanced baseline. The affected sites were replication, voter, merge-change, deploy, the shared deferral/interrupt helper, and G2P in infra/scripts/observability.sh.\n\nProof: whole-script PATH-shim experiments started each stream at offset 2/source total 7 and forced the targeted AWS call to exit 23. Before repair every stream advanced to 7 and the retry published 0; retaining 2 made the retry publish 5. The reset control reproduced 7 then 0 from offset 10/source 7. Removing only stderr/error suppression did not recover the count, ruling out suppression as a second cause.\n\nTest: tests/scripts/test_observability_offsets_6a65.py was observed RED before repair through the real script, GREEN after repair, and RED again when the exact pre-acknowledgement mutation was restored. After restoring the fix, 10 focused observability tests pass.\n\nFix: Gerrit 1566, commit e701e053a28d244ee639804d501c5dc6198b2d65, merged after LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and zero unresolved comments. Each stream now advances its offset only inside the successful AWS branch. AWS failure remains best-effort for the systemd probe, but the count remains unacknowledged for retry.\n\nScope and safety: caller sweep found no consumer relying on premature acknowledgement. The change restores the original epic contracts that observed failures publish metrics and trip alarms, adds no dependency, preserves exit-zero, reset, and zero-delta behavior, and weakens no existing test. make lint and make typecheck pass.\n\nSiblings: the construct sweep found and fixed all seven live streams, including the previously omitted G2P stream and both shared-helper metrics. Parity census: CLI/MCP/library surfaces are N/A for this shell probe; automated systemd/autodeploy callers share the repaired script; the read/write dual direction is N/A beyond source-counter reads and CloudWatch publication.\n\nResidual risk and prevention: fixed in scope by the parameterized whole-script regression across every stream. No additional observed fragility remains undispositioned.\n\nReplication: for every targeted stream, a forced first publish failure leaves the offset byte-identical, the second successful run republishes the accumulated delta, and only then advances the offset. The original report no longer reproduces. Ticket intentionally remains in_progress per session directive.","timestamp":1786303034743689001}],"created_at":1786121556322032001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ac14be90-d92c-40e0-8b97-cd3a3241b08c","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"9f63-16dc-f014-4df2"},{"link_uuid":"fc9c11a1-6ed8-429a-b6f6-c4f6a1e6bc09","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"346c-8bf9-02c9-457e"}],"description":"## Context\n\nCumulative error counters in infra/scripts/observability.sh persist an acknowledgement offset before CloudWatch accepts the matching datapoint. A transient put-metric-data failure therefore causes the next interval to compute zero from an already-advanced baseline, permanently losing the positive delta. The same copied construct affects seven metric streams across six code shapes, including the G2P block omitted from the original five-site census.\n\n## Proven root cause\n\nEach affected block writes total to its offset file before running aws cloudwatch put-metric-data. Whole-script runtime probes showed offset 2/source 7/failing AWS becomes offset 7, and the next successful run publishes 0 rather than 5 for every stream. Removing only error suppression does not recover the count. Original feature stories explicitly require these observed failures to publish metrics and trip alarms.\n\n## Repair plan\n\n- Reorder each of the six concrete publish shapes so the matching offset advances only after a successful CloudWatch call. Cover replication, voter, merge-change, deploy, both shared autodeploy-marker streams, and G2P.\n- Preserve the script systemd exit-0 contract and existing logging behavior: AWS failure stays best-effort for the overall probe, but the failed metric remains unacknowledged.\n- Keep zero-delta publication behavior unchanged; a successful zero publish may acknowledge the observed total. Preserve reset handling where total below offset retries total.\n- Add a whole-script PATH-shim regression oracle that drives the real script, fails each targeted AWS metric once, proves the offset is byte-identical after failure, then proves a successful retry publishes the accumulated delta and advances the offset. Include zero/reset controls and both shared-helper metrics.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Run `pytest -q tests/scripts/test_observability_offsets_6a65.py tests/scripts/test_observability_exit.py`.\n- Run `make lint` and `make typecheck`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] All seven cumulative counter streams advance their offset only after the matching successful AWS publication, checked by the whole-script test.\n- [x] A failed publication leaves the targeted offset byte-identical, checked for every stream by the whole-script test.\n- [x] A subsequent successful run publishes the accumulated delta and then advances the offset, checked for every stream.\n- [x] Reset handling retries the reset total after failure, and zero-delta behavior remains compatible.\n- [x] observability.sh still exits zero when an individual AWS publication fails and on a healthy run.\n- [x] The held-out oracle is observed RED before the fix, GREEN after the fix, and RED again under the original pre-acknowledgement mutation.\n- [x] Repository lint and typecheck gates pass.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/scripts/observability.sh","reason":"Persist each cumulative-counter offset only after its matching CloudWatch publication succeeds."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_observability_offsets_6a65.py","reason":"Held-out whole-script failure/retry oracle across all seven metric streams plus zero/reset controls."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_observability_exit.py","reason":"Retain and, if needed, extend the systemd exit-zero compatibility control."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","346c-8bf9-02c9-457e"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"8f300cc3-a43f-40dc-94b9-e097e5aae699","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"6a65-25b5-b5c3-436d","ticket_type":"bug","title":"observability.sh advances its metric offset before the CloudWatch publish, so a transient put-metric-data failure permanently loses that interval's count","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b5a097a7-bf20-4a9c-8d45-682d9e0e79b5","ac14be90-d92c-40e0-8b97-cd3a3241b08c","5b151e25-1520-4df1-aec3-091cd0c58630","6134aa33-a85e-48a4-a093-b79744cf204f","ead73741-f942-481f-96fe-869f6ea06675","5dc28f6a-9655-4d09-a040-7c8d0226a996","3f5c1a8b-ed53-4d86-a689-543c1aa85315","1b9c75f9-b637-4519-9c5d-98cb05c0765d","dd38fb4b-c794-425d-acab-968db3681da7","35bc29b0-1714-48bf-bc16-614dd20cf6f1","fc9c11a1-6ed8-429a-b6f6-c4f6a1e6bc09","32961542-1d37-4055-a93b-71174dc3400b","f843f4c6-3cdd-4b8a-943f-5779ab447cec","8f300cc3-a43f-40dc-94b9-e097e5aae699","0b1b24a9-3320-47d0-b333-4e1f6f1070f9"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659615697880001,"uuid":"005d5421-7ead-44bd-8678-1ad89a45002a"}